From 5bd5725a5724c423dd914d6c78db75292453fe42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Gagne <kgagne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:50:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add an optional Space preview command for the folder view

Pressing Space in the folder view runs the command set as preview_cmd in
the [config] group of pcmanfm.conf on the selected items, so a
quick-look style previewer can show files without opening them. The
command takes desktop entry field codes: %F or %U receive every selected
item, %f or %u run it once per item, and GLib adds %f when it has none.
The launch uses the display's app launch context, so the previewer gets
startup notification and activation.

Only plain Space is taken, and only while the folder view has focus.
With nothing selected, the item under the keyboard cursor is selected
and previewed, so Space acts on the row with the focus outline instead
of opening it. The location bar, rename and search entries keep Space.
Without preview_cmd, Space behaves exactly as before.
---
 data/pcmanfm.1.in |  9 ++++++
 src/app-config.c  |  5 ++++
 src/app-config.h  |  2 ++
 src/main-win.c    | 71 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 87 insertions(+)

diff --git a/data/pcmanfm.1.in b/data/pcmanfm.1.in
index b1187d2..b6464eb 100644
--- a/data/pcmanfm.1.in
+++ b/data/pcmanfm.1.in
@@ -101,6 +101,15 @@ of icons resembles folder view in main window of \fBpcmanfm\fP but icons on
 desktop can "remember" their position. If you have two or more monitors then
 desktop background and set of icons will be shown on each of them. Icons
 positions will be remembered individually for each of monitors.
+
+Pressing Space in the folder view can preview the selected items without
+opening them, if a preview command is set as \fBpreview_cmd\fP in the
+[config] group of \fIpcmanfm.conf\fP, for example
+\fBpreview_cmd=my\-previewer %F\fP. The command takes the field codes of a
+desktop entry's Exec key: %F or %U receive every selected item as paths or
+URIs, while %f or %u run the command once per item; %f is added when it has
+none. With nothing selected, Space selects and previews the item under the
+keyboard cursor. Without \fBpreview_cmd\fP Space keeps its usual meaning.
 .SH ENVIRONMENT
 .PD 0
 .TP
